      <item>
        <title>RT by @ylecun: Reactions to this tweet reveal the lack of understanding of sources of American economic dynamism among the political right. Saying “we’ve always had the best American workers before” ignores how many of our top firms came from immigrants. That’s always been our advantage.</title>
        <dc:creator>@C_Garthwaite</dc:creator>
        <description><![CDATA[<p>Reactions to this tweet reveal the lack of understanding of sources of American economic dynamism among the political right.<br>
<br>
Saying “we’ve always had the best American workers before” ignores how many of our top firms came from immigrants.<br>
<br>
That’s always been our advantage.</p>
<hr/>
<blockquote>
<b>Craig Garthwaite (@C_Garthwaite)</b>
<p>
<p>This might be one of the worst self inflicted wounds we could create. <br>
<br>
Even contemplating it causes damage. <br>
<br>
The strength of our economy has always come from taking the best and brightest of the world and putting them to work.</p>
<img src="https://nitter.net/pic/media%2FHOfupngWUAASOo0.jpg" style="max-width:250px;" />


</p>
<footer>
— <cite><a href="https://nitter.net/C_Garthwaite/status/2082895754092220423#m">https://nitter.net/C_Garthwaite/status/2082895754092220423#m</a>
</footer>
</blockquote>]]></description>
